{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775480832,"nonce":"I00+OFNvgAWKGpoBwlUQsXpx/6w=","title":"Add date filtering and cross-project aggregation to nightshift usage","message":"Add date filtering and cross-project aggregation to nightshift usage command\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_usage_since_filter\n  Assert: entries before --since date are excluded from output\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_usage_until_filter\n  Assert: entries after --until date are excluded from output\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_usage_since_and_until\n  Assert: only entries within the date range are shown\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_usage_daily_summary\n  Assert: --daily groups entries by date with per-day subtotals\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_usage_all_projects\n  Assert: --all-projects scans ~/src/*/.nightshift/usage.jsonl and aggregates by project\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_usage_all_projects_with_date_filter\n  Assert: --all-projects combined with --since/--until filters correctly\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_cmd_usage_no_matching_entries\n  Assert: prints \"No matching usage entries.\" when filters exclude everything\n\n## Files\n- host/cli.py (modify — update cmd_usage and its argparse registration)\n\n## Implementation\n1. Add helper `_parse_date(s)` that calls `datetime.date.fromisoformat(s)` for YYYY-MM-DD strings.\n2. Add helper `_entry_date(entry)` that extracts a `datetime.date` from an entry's `completed_at` or `started_at` field (tries both, returns None if neither parses).\n3. Add helper `_load_usage_entries(usage_file)` that reads JSONL and returns list of dicts (moves existing code out of cmd_usage).\n4. Add helper `_filter_entries(entries, issue_id=None, since=None, until=None)` that filters by issue_id prefix and date range.\n5. Add helper `_print_entries(entries)` that prints the per-entry table and totals (moves existing code out of cmd_usage).\n6. Add helper `_print_daily_summary(entries)` that groups entries by date, prints per-day subtotals (sessions count, tokens in/out, cost), then grand total.\n7. Add `_cmd_usage_all_projects(a, since, until)` that scans `~/src/*/.nightshift/usage.jsonl`, loads and filters each, then prints per-project summary (project name, session count, tokens, cost) and grand total. If `--daily` is also set, prints daily summary across all projects.\n8. Update `cmd_usage(a)` to parse `a.since`, `a.until`, check `a.all_projects` and `a.daily`, delegate to helpers.\n9. Update argparse registration for \"usage\" subcommand: add `--since` (YYYY-MM-DD), `--until` (YYYY-MM-DD), `--daily` (flag), `--all-projects` (flag).\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee existing `cmd_usage` in `host/cli.py` for the current implementation pattern.\nSee `format_token_count` from `core/post_run.py` for token formatting.\nSee `_load_usage_entries` pattern: read file, splitlines, json.loads each, skip malformed with warning.\n\n## Notes\n- Date comparison uses `datetime.date` objects, not string comparison.\n- `--all-projects` hardcodes `~/src/` as the parent directory (consistent with the shell one-liner for counting trajectories).\n- Helpers are module-private (prefixed with `_`) since they're only used by cmd_usage.\n- Keep functions under 50 lines per CLAUDE.md rules.\n\nREQ: REQ-032","files":null}]}